ae\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Orchidaceae\">orchid</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hybrid_(biology)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Hybrid (biology)\">Hybrid</a> <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Dactylorhiza_%C3%97_braunii\" title=\"Dactylorhiza × braunii\">Dactylorhiza × braunii</a> is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hybrid_(biology)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Hybrid (biology)\">Hybrid</a> by <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_spotted_orchid\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Common spotted orchid\">Common Spotted-orchid (Dactylorhiza fuchsii)</a></i> and <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_marsh_orchid\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Western marsh orchid\">Western marsh orchid (Dactylorhiza majalis; also broad-leaved marsh orchid, fan orchid, common marsh orchid, Irish Marsh-orchid)</a></i>. This image shows one of the rarest plants worldwide. There is only a little number of habitats worldwide. For example: Great Britain has 6 habitats, Ireland 2 habitats, Bavaria 1 habitat. The Global Biodiversity information Facility says: there are only 11 number of occurences by 8 data providers in europe."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1988"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Michael_G%C3%A4bler\" title=\"User:Michael Gäbler\">Michael Gäbler</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":26612652,"title":"File:Dactylorhiza incarnata hybrid - kahkjaspunase sõrmkäpa hübriid.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Dactylorhiza_incarnata_hybrid_-_kahkjaspunase_s%C3%B5rmk%C3%A4pa_h%C3%BCbriid.jpg/960px-Dactylorhiza_incarnata_hybrid_-_kahkjaspunase_s%C3%B5rmk%C3%A4pa_h%C3%BCbriid.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dactylorhiza_incarnata_hybrid_-_kahkjaspunase_s%C3%B5rmk%C3%A4pa_h%C3%BCbriid.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":